Changelog: 09-10-2026 21:33:27

BC-250 BIOS Reader is now a card in the portal (bios-reader-v0.1.0, read-only, no board warning).

Changelog: 09-10-2026 17:59:08

Update notices: a red dot on every card whose installed app differs from the version this portal pins (the Update
case), a red count in the header ("1 update"), and a check at start for a newer portal release on GitHub (tags
portal-v*, in the background with bc250_core.updates; nothing shows when offline or when there is none). A newer one
shows a red "Portal x.y.z available" button that opens its release page. Tests in tests/test_window.py.

Changelog: 09-10-2026 17:51:51

Only one instance runs per user: starting the app again brings the running window to the front instead of opening a second one.

Changelog: 09-10-2026 16:28:35

apps.toml: new card for BC-250 System Overlay (system-overlay-v0.1.0), without the board warning: it only
reads sensors.

Changelog: 09-10-2026 13:56:58

apps.toml: Persistent ACPI now installs its app (bash install.sh, no sudo) instead of the ACPI override, is
detected by its launcher and gets an Open button. The override is installed from the app's window. The portal
test that used Persistent ACPI as the app without an Open button now uses a changed copy of another entry.

Changelog: 09-10-2026 12:15:17

A portal installed from the suite checkout now installs the other apps from that checkout as well, as it already
did when run from there. Before, it fell back to the GitHub releases, so the optional apps could not be tried
before they were released. install.sh records the checkout in /opt/bc250-bazzite-suite/suite-checkout; an install
from a release has no such file and is unchanged.

Changelog: 08-10-2026 22:26:29

Initial release 0.1.0 of the BC250 Bazzite Suite portal.

One window for the suite's apps. BC-250 Bazzite Test comes first and is always installed. The other apps
(governor, helixsr, cu-bisect, cores-bisect, gpu-oc-bisect, persistent-acpi) are cards with Install, Open and
Uninstall:
- Each runs the app's own installer in a terminal window and watches for its result.
- Apps that change how the board runs are marked, and the portal asks for confirmation before installing or
  opening them.

apps.toml pins one release of each app. The portal downloads exactly that tarball from the suite's releases,
checks it against the pinned SHA-256 (or the release's SHA256SUMS) and unpacks it safely. Run from a checkout,
it installs apps from the local source instead.

install.sh installs the portal root-owned to /opt/bc250-bazzite-suite, sets up the suite's shared venv and
installs the bundled BC-250 Bazzite Test release.
